Package: wb-node-red
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 nodejs (>= 22.9)
Recommends: nginx, mosquitto, wb-mqtt-homeui (>= 2.241.0)
Description: Node-RED for Wiren Board controllers (native)
 Runs Node-RED natively on the controller host as a systemd service, with a
 default flow pre-wired to the local MQTT broker on localhost:1883 and the
 device tree (/devices/#).
 .
 Node-RED is vendored into the package at build time, so no
 npm download or native compilation happens on the controller; Node.js comes
 from the distribution (Depends: nodejs) so its security updates flow from the
 Wiren Board / Debian repository.
 .
 The service runs as a dedicated unprivileged user with the editor bound to
 loopback and reverse-proxied on a dedicated HTTPS port (21880) behind the homeui
 login (admin only); the old /node-red/ path is kept as a redirect to that port.
 User data persists across upgrades; both it and the runtime tree live under
 /mnt/data (surviving a firmware re-flash). Updates are explicit (the package
 is excluded from unattended-upgrades).
